95991b7852b855","changed":false,"changed_paths":[],"commit":"fa4e7c7125fe619b5490ff11fbf3823148854e19","commits":[],"cumulative_patch_sha256":"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855","finding_commits":{},"parent":"fa4e7c7125fe619b5490ff11fbf3823148854e19","patch_sha256":"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855","tree":"592c362bbfd8eab4b238eb1588c1267d13226e00"},"dispositions":{"comments":[{"body":"[P2] [Javaagent] Restore the empty context for untraced stashed messages\n\n`PekkoStashBufferNodeInstrumentation` leaves the node's virtual field unset when the stashing context is `Context.root()`. If that message is later unstashed by a message carrying an `unlock` span, `switchTo(null)` closes the previous scope but opens no replacement, so the unstashed handler runs under the unlock context. Its spans and baggage are consequently attributed to the unrelated unlock operation rather than the context in which it was stashed. This also occurs when an untraced message follows a traced message in the same stash. Treat a missing node context as `Context.root()` and scope it during interpretation; add an agent-backed regression covering an untraced message and a mixed traced/untraced stash. The frozen helper reproduces this: after switching from a parent context to null under an unlock context, `Context.current()` is still the unlock context.","line":23,"path":"instrumentation/pekko/pekko-actor-1.0/javaagent/src/main/java/io/opentelemetry/javaagent/instrumentation/pekkoactor/v1_0/typed/UnstashScope.java","side":"RIGHT"}],"input_identity":{"pr_diff_sha256":"7701e8c594397a3d9e9fcd3a2e5e0de2bd178d74534d4e872abc946a8fef85fd"},"outcome":"comments","request_digest":"b65784dd5e3b1fd5f5bc08d316d389059fb71a00c6568cf93d59e8ad1244b610","schema":2},"download_sha256":"feb305d37ada220488606b15b3d70266eaf342bf53fcc49d31248a59eb28c9c5","frozen_sha":"fa4e7c7125fe619b5490ff11fbf3823148854e19","pr":20528,"publication_eligible":false,"repo":"open